  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(k + 1/k)² = 9\n\n**Formula used:**\n\n(k³ + 1/k³) = (k + 1/k)³ - 3(k + 1/k)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n(k + 1/k)2 = 9\n\nk + 1/k = 3\n\n(k3 + 1/k3) = (k + 1/k)3 - 3(k + 1/k)\n\n(k3 + 1/k3) = (3)3 - 3(3)\n\n(k3 + 1/k3) = 27 - 9\n\n(k3 + 1/k3) = 18\n\n**∴ Option 2 is the correct answer.**",
